{"page":205,"blocks":[{"x":0.65814,"y":0.05257,"w":0.29337,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"3.9 Inverse Trigonometric Functions 191"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.093,"w":0.47882,"h":0.01375,"fs":0.01375,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Derivatives of the Other Three Inverse Trigonometric Functions"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.11766,"w":0.59297,"h":0.04348,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"We could use the same techniques to find the derivatives of the other three inverse trigono- metric functions—arccosine, arccotangent, and arccosecant—but there is an easier way, thanks to the following identities."},{"x":0.39285,"y":0.2188,"w":0.32872,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Inverse Function–Inverse Cofunction Identities"},{"x":0.57568,"y":0.23141,"w":0.16131,"h":0.02323,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"cos-1x = p>2 - sin-1x"},{"x":0.57589,"y":0.25059,"w":0.16329,"h":0.04241,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"cot-1x = p>2 - tan-1x csc-1x = p>2 - sec-1x"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.34761,"w":0.59306,"h":0.05883,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"We saw the first of these identities in Equation (5) of Section 1.6. The others are derived in a similar way. It follows easily that the derivatives of the inverse cofunctions are the negatives of the derivatives of the corresponding inverse functions. For example, the derivative of cos-1x is calculated as follows:"},{"x":0.59294,"y":0.41301,"w":0.03962,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx ap"},{"x":0.62273,"y":0.41301,"w":0.15902,"h":0.03044,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"2 - sin-1xb Identity"},{"x":0.49272,"y":0.41623,"w":0.11202,"h":0.0276,"fs":0.01401,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"d dx (cos-1x) = d"},{"x":0.57587,"y":0.45204,"w":0.04223,"h":0.01999,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= - d"},{"x":0.6063,"y":0.45737,"w":0.07258,"h":0.02227,"fs":0.01401,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx (sin-1x)"},{"x":0.57587,"y":0.48803,"w":0.06595,"h":0.01914,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"= - 1"},{"x":0.60794,"y":0.49507,"w":0.24167,"h":0.02364,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"21 - x2. Derivative of arcsine"},{"x":0.39203,"y":0.52832,"w":0.5435,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The derivatives of the inverse trigonometric functions are summarized in Table 3.1."},{"x":0.38221,"y":0.59987,"w":0.4104,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"TABLE 3.1 Derivatives of the inverse trigonometric functions"},{"x":0.5043,"y":0.64518,"w":0.15739,"h":0.03674,"fs":0.01353,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"21 - u2 du dx, 0 u0 6 1"},{"x":0.38221,"y":0.6471,"w":0.09512,"h":0.02394,"fs":0.01401,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"1. d(sin-1u)"},{"x":0.43799,"y":0.65124,"w":0.1003,"h":0.0271,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"dx = 1"},{"x":0.52006,"y":0.68483,"w":0.15739,"h":0.03674,"fs":0.01353,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"21 - u2 du dx, 0 u0 6 1"},{"x":0.38221,"y":0.68675,"w":0.09751,"h":0.02394,"fs":0.01401,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"2. d(cos-1u)"},{"x":0.43918,"y":0.69089,"w":0.11486,"h":0.02709,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"dx = - 1"},{"x":0.38222,"y":0.7264,"w":0.09595,"h":0.02394,"fs":0.01401,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"3. d(tan-1u)"},{"x":0.4384,"y":0.73035,"w":0.13161,"h":0.0289,"fs":0.01279,"n":6,"k":0,"t":"dx = 1 1 + u2 du dx"},{"x":0.38221,"y":0.76604,"w":0.09596,"h":0.02394,"fs":0.01401,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"4. d(cot-1u)"},{"x":0.4384,"y":0.77,"w":0.14497,"h":0.0289,"fs":0.01279,"n":6,"k":0,"t":"dx = - 1 1 + u2 du dx"},{"x":0.43908,"y":0.80249,"w":0.2449,"h":0.03674,"fs":0.01353,"n":7,"k":0,"t":"dx = 1 0 u0 2u2 - 1 du dx, 0 u0 7 1"},{"x":0.38221,"y":0.80441,"w":0.09731,"h":0.02394,"fs":0.01401,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"5. d(sec-1u)"},{"x":0.43908,"y":0.84597,"w":0.25827,"h":0.03674,"fs":0.01353,"n":7,"k":0,"t":"dx = - 1 0 u0 2u2 - 1 du dx, 0 u0 7 1"},{"x":0.38222,"y":0.84789,"w":0.0973,"h":0.02394,"fs":0.01401,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"6. d(csc-1u)"}]}